        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left heel pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pain at the anteromedial heel for about 3–4 weeks, described as like standing on a stone. Worse on the first steps in the morning and after long periods sitting in a patrol car; eases after 10–15 minutes walking, then becomes a dull ache by the end of the shift. Worse with long shifts, foot patrol, and heavy boots."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
